<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leszek the White</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1184–1227</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Leszek I the White</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leszek the White was a Piast duke of Sandomierz and, with interruptions, high duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> from 1194 until his death. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-ii-the-just">Casimir II the Just</a>, he struggled with his uncle Mieszko III and other relatives for the senior throne, and he intervened repeatedly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. He was killed at Gąsawa in 1227 during an assembly of Piast dukes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white.jpg" alt="Leszek the White" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Zuber at Polish Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piecz%C4%99%C4%87_Leszka_I_Bia%C5%82ego.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
